<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak Slovnaft SKK 1.3 bln 96 net profit.</title>
<headline>Slovak Slovnaft SKK 1.3 bln 96 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audited results for year ending December 31, 1996:</p>
<p>(in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	2.307     vs    3.274</p>
<p> Net profit	    1.290     vs    1.828</p>
<p> Operating revenues		   39.438    vs	35.102</p>
<p> Operating costs			36.520    vs	31.765</p>
<p> Revenues from financial	     0.872    vs	 0.699</p>
<p>operations</p>
<p> Financial costs			 1.476    vs	 0.658</p>
<p>Revenue from regular</p>
<p>  activities			    40.310    vs	35.801</p>
<p> Costs of regular activities	37.996    vs	32.423</p>
<p> Total turnover			 40.310    vs	35.820</p>
<p>Revenues from own operations</p>
<p>  and sales of products	     35.889    vs	31.917</p>
<p> Total exports			  17.609    vs	15.600</p>
<p> Overall tax			     1.020    vs	 1.440</p>
<p> External sources		     13.637    vs	 9.246</p>
<p> Reserves				  0.764    vs	 0.676</p>
<p> Long-term liabilities		 0.0	vs	 0.019</p>
<p> Short-term liabilities		4.420    vs	 4.523</p>
<p> Total bank loans			8.453    vs	 4.028</p>
<p> Long-term claims			0.430    vs	 0.745</p>
<p> Short-term claims		     4.448    vs	 5.243</p>
<p> Financial investment		  3.961    vs	 3.366</p>
<p>Volume of processed</p>
<p> materials (in million of tonnes)  5.421    vs	 5.381</p>
<p>Volume of processed</p>
<p> crude oil (million tonnes)	  5.180    vs	 5.108</p>
<p> Basic capital			  16.469    vs	16.469</p>
<p> Total assets			   37.927    vs	32.507</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Slovnaft a.s. Results are consolidated and audited.</p>
<p>Slovnaft officials said that the lower pre-tax profit in 1996 was due mainly to increases in world crude oil prices which were not offset by a corresponding increase in prices of Slovnaft products and because of lower working time due to general maintenance.</p>
<p>Slovnaft is Slovakia's sole crude oil refiner controlling around 80 percent of the domestic petrol station market. The company shut 70 percent of its refining capacity from early March to the end of April to complete major maintenence.</p>
<p>Slovnaft's main shareholders as of December 31, 1996, were Slovintegra a.s. with 39.00 percent, the state through the National Property Fund (19.15 percent), the Bank of New York with 10.53 percent, and Benzinol a.s. 5.84 percent.</p>
<p>-- Peter Javurek, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-521-8402</p>
